    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "100ae8f84f68d6166783d08c8b39e73d4c56063211795b2d20cc07f710047062",
      "text": "Set out for the ruins of Calakmul. Once a powerful Maya city and the capital of the Kaanul kingdom, Calakmul was a political rival of Tikal. It reached its peak between 200 and 700 CE.\n\nThe American Cyrus Lundell discovered Calakmul, also known as Kaan or the “Snake Kingdom,” in 1931. The city covered about 30 km², with more than 100 major structures and around 5,000 buildings in all.\n\nTwo pyramids, known as Structure I and Structure II, stand out at around 45 meters high. The largest pyramid measures 140 meters along one side.\n\nAfter visiting the ruins, continue to Palenque. Check in at a four-star hotel and stay overnight in Palenque.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw6lz405-1ivofn2o2t2",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      }
